# @colis Issue Triage — Packages Repo Rule

This rule applies to AI agents working **inside this monorepo** (`weitzmany/colis`).
It defines the full issue lifecycle from triage to resolution.

## Reading Open Issues

Use the `list_issues` MCP tool to see what is open:

```
list_issues({ status: "open" })
list_issues({ package: "@colis/keel", type: "bug" })
```

Or use the GitHub CLI directly for detailed inspection:

```bash
gh issue list --repo weitzmany/colis --state open
gh issue view 42 --repo weitzmany/colis --json number,title,body,labels,author,state,createdAt
# fallback when gh issue view hits deprecated project fields:
gh api repos/weitzmany/colis/issues/42
```

Always fetch all open issues by state first, then classify by labels. Do not rely on `status:*` labels being present.

## Issue Lifecycle

```
status:open → status:in-progress → status:resolved → (opener closes)
```

### 1. Acknowledge (status:open → status:in-progress)

When you start working on an issue, update its label:

```bash
gh issue edit <number> --repo weitzmany/colis \
  --remove-label "status:open" \
  --add-label "status:in-progress"
gh issue comment <number> --repo weitzmany/colis \
  --body "Acknowledged — investigating."
```

### 2. Resolve (status:in-progress → status:resolved + status:awaiting-confirmation)

After shipping a fix, mark the issue resolved and notify the opener:

```bash
gh issue edit <number> --repo weitzmany/colis \
  --remove-label "status:in-progress" \
  --add-label "status:resolved,status:awaiting-confirmation"
gh issue comment <number> --repo weitzmany/colis \
  --body "Fixed in @colis/<package> v<X.Y.Z>. Please update the package in your project and confirm the fix works, then close this issue."
```

### 3. Close — Opener Only

**Do NOT close issues yourself.** The consuming project that filed the issue
must close it after confirming the fix. Adding a comment asking them to do so is correct.

If an issue has been `status:awaiting-confirmation` for more than two weeks with no response,
you may add a comment noting you'll close it if there's no reply within 48 hours — but do not
close it unilaterally without explicit user approval.

## Commit Message Safety

**Never write commit messages that trigger GitHub's automatic issue closing.**

GitHub closes issues automatically when merges to the default branch contain:
- `fixes #<n>`, `fix #<n>`, `fixed #<n>`
- `closes #<n>`, `close #<n>`, `closed #<n>`
- `resolves #<n>`, `resolve #<n>`, `resolved #<n>`

Use neutral references instead:

```bash
# ✅ Safe — reference without trigger
git commit -m "fix(keel): improve button contrast (see #42)"

# ✅ Safe — package-scoped reference
git commit -m "fix(@colis/keel): address accessibility contrast issue #42"

# ❌ Dangerous — auto-closes the issue
git commit -m "fix(keel): improve button contrast, closes #42"
```

## Publishing After a Fix

After resolving an issue and publishing the fix:

1. Update the issue comment with the exact version that contains the fix.
2. Change label to `status:resolved` + `status:awaiting-confirmation`.
3. Wait for the consuming project to verify and close the issue.

## Label Reference

| Label | Who Sets It | Meaning |
|-------|------------|---------|
| `status:open` | reporter (MCP tool) | Filed, not yet acknowledged |
| `status:in-progress` | packages repo LLM | Actively being worked on |
| `status:resolved` | packages repo LLM | Fix shipped |
| `status:awaiting-confirmation` | packages repo LLM | Waiting for opener to close |
| `source:ai-agent` | reporter (MCP tool) | Filed by a Cursor agent |
| `type:bug` | reporter | Bug report |
| `type:feature-request` | reporter | Feature request |
| `package:*` | reporter | Affected package |

## Triage Priority

1. `type:bug` + `status:open` — highest priority, breaks consuming projects
2. `type:feature-request` + `status:open` — review and plan
3. `type:question` — answer in a comment and close when resolved

When multiple bugs are open, fix them in dependency order:
- Core packages (`@colis/rig`) first
- Then leaf packages (`@colis/keel`, `@colis/hull`, etc.)
